The Weierstrass Institute for Applied Analysis and Stochastics (WIAS) is an institute of the Forschungsverbund Berlin e.V. (FVB). The FVB comprises seven non-university research institutes in Berlin which are funded by the federal and state governments. The research institutes belong to the Leibniz Association.

WIAS invites applications for a

**Research Assistant Position (f/m/d)**

**(Ref. 26/22)**

in the Research Group “**Nonsmooth Variational Problems and Operator Equations**”

(Head: Prof. Dr. Michael Hintermüller), starting on **January 1, 2027**.

**Field of work:**

The successful candidate will work in the MATH+ project "DOC-TWIN: Duality-Based Error Control for Optimal Control Problems in Digital-Twin-Based Structural Health Monitoring". The project aims at developing a convex-duality-based framework for reliable error control in PDE-constrained optimal control problems motivated by digital-twin-based structural health monitoring.

**The Tasks include:**

* Developing and analyzing duality-based a posteriori error identities for PDE-constrained optimal control problems;
* Deriving corresponding discrete a priori error identities and using them for convergence-rate analysis and certified nonlinear solver control;
